Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Bondi k-Calculus: Special Relativity in the Euclidean Plane", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"4ddb5767-1f00-4973-a411-49eacd07850d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Bondi's k-calculus derives special relativity from one number: two inertial \
observers who meet at an event, and one sends light signals at proper-time \
interval ",
 StyleBox["T", "TI"],
 ", the other receives them at interval ",
 StyleBox["kT", "TI"],
 ". Everything below follows from ",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 " and the radar rule."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"2b769789-0097-45cb-acd5-812650f8aaa5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The constructions are drawn in the Euclidean plane: the observer at rest is \
the time axis, an observer of velocity ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " is a straight ray from the same origin, and light runs at a fixed angle ",
 StyleBox["\[CurlyPhi]", "TI"],
 " to the time axis. The k-factor appears as a ratio of arc lengths."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bddd3932-6c51-45e0-8b43-d5ac96769b45"],

Cell["\<\
The order is the order of the k-calculus: the k-factor and the Doppler \
effect, radar time and distance, time dilation, simultaneity, length \
contraction, velocity addition, the light clock, and the Bondi clock, whose \
bounces grow geometrically.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"f6531b04-cb04-45f5-afc8-600ccb18e97b"],

Cell["\<\
The functions take no graph; units have the speed of light 1. The figures are \
experimental: each claim made from a figure below is checked on the \
primitives it draws.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5dc2a58b-0e51-4eb0-9477-ba49598d0325"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"31ca4d3f-5966-4b74-9759-dca8c36382a8"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<WolframInstitute`InfraGeometry`\>\"", "]"}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<WolframInstitute`InfraCausality`\>\"", 
  "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"fa76346e-d83a-4c7f-b13e-64f856a733a6"],

Cell["The Euclidean picture", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"504a34b1-3986-42f1-aee7-b0266afeece7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The rest observer, Alice, is the time axis {0, 1}. The observer of velocity \
",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ", Bob, is the ray at the angle ",
 StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"],
 " = arctan(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " tan ",
 StyleBox["\[CurlyPhi]", "TI"],
 ") of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["WorldlineAngle"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/WorldlineAngle", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9cae15b0-4544-4bbc-bbe9-c169d3c0edb9"],
 ", with direction (sin ",
 StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"],
 ", cos ",
 StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"],
 "); light runs along the two directions (\[PlusMinus]sin ",
 StyleBox["\[CurlyPhi]", "TI"],
 ", cos ",
 StyleBox["\[CurlyPhi]", "TI"],
 "). The light angle is a choice of drawing: ",
 StyleBox["\[CurlyPhi]", "TI"],
 " = \[Pi]/4 is the usual Minkowski diagram, and the other angles rescale the \
space axis."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b78728e2-303b-4687-915e-120feedabc13"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Alice (blue), Bob at ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " = 0.6 (red) and the two light directions (yellow), at the light angles \
\[Pi]/4 and \[Pi]/3."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7ed1393a-7581-497a-aea5-d7998365d7eb"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

